# Documentation archive policy (ARCHIVE-POLICY-001)

## Purpose

`docs/archive/<program_id>/` holds **immutable historical** documentation that
must remain searchable but is **not** active authority. Active authority lives
only in [`docs/index.yaml`](../index.yaml).

## Rules

1. **No bulk blind moves.** Phase trees move program-by-program with an
   inventory row and `superseded_by` on the replacement (or an explicit
   `status: archived` index entry).
2. **Archive is immutable.** Do not edit archived content except to fix
   broken relative links after a move (link-fix commits only).
3. **Inbound links from active docs** may point at archive for history; they
   must not treat archive as the sole SoT for a live concern.
4. **Ignored scratch (`TEMP/`, `temp/`, `tmp/`, `.tmp/`)** is never archive.
   Promote first (PSR-2b) or drop authority links (PSR-2c); do not `git add`
   TEMP/tmp scratch.
5. **Root local-ops notes are not archive.** Machine-specific SSH / VS Code /
   host-connection guides must not live at the monorepo root and must not be
   relocated into `docs/archive/` (they are not program authority). Remove them
   from the tree; recover from git history only if needed.
6. **PSR-2c pilot:** root-command satellite worksheets →
   [`psr-001/root-command/`](./psr-001/root-command/). Full `docs/phase-*`
   relocation remains a follow-on slice after link hygiene is green.

## Layout

```text
docs/archive/
  README.mdoc                 # this index pointer
  ARCHIVE-POLICY via standard above
  psr-001/
    root-command/             # 15 ROOT_COMMAND_* worksheets (PSR-2c)
  root-forensics/             # former monorepo-root audit/health reports
    # future: phase-N/ … when scheduled
```

### `root-forensics/` (Wave-1 hygiene)

Immutable copies of reports that previously cluttered the monorepo root
(`ENTERPRISE_AUDIT_REPORT.md`, `audit-red-flags-phase-*.md`,
`SYSTEM_HEALTH_REPORT.md`, etc.). They remain searchable historical evidence.
Active authority stays in phase guides, MAP, and `docs/audits/` / live guards —
do not treat `root-forensics/` as SoT for open remediation work.
